      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T01:42:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To save the latest frame, we don\u0027t need to save \"every\" frame. Before Ferrochrome becomes invisible, onPause and onStop callbacks are triggered. I think we can capture the frame only at the moment, and use the captured frame later when it is resumed (onResume). \n\nOr, a simpler approach might be sending out a harmless input event upon resuming, so that the guest OS updates the screen.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "a468073a323990bc6cf6e280bdf83779d6e6a073",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15cc948a_e619f081",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561731
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T23:19:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that the guest may be \"stable\" when onPause/onStop are called and may not be producing new frames (maybe Chrome is paused while showing a fullscreen Youtube video, it may not be generating any new frames).\n\n\u003e a simpler approach might be sending out a harmless input event upon resuming\n\nI believe we considered this approach for CF as well but I think we decided that we did not know what input event to send that would be guaranteed to be harmless and not mess with the existing guest state.",
      "parentUuid": "23850bca_3598e43a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "a468073a323990bc6cf6e280bdf83779d6e6a073",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4be59c92_fcae3e90",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-02T06:56:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It could be a meta key event like alt, shift, or fn, or a seldom-used event like numlock(twice). I know; not ideal, but good enough as a temporary fix.\n\nMore ideally, going out of the VM and then coming back should be seen as a resume-after-sleep, which I believe the OS will anyway draw a frame even without an input event.",
      "parentUuid": "15cc948a_e619f081",
